WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.949
In Final Destination, those who escaped fatal
accidents are now in a race against death

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:06.840
to find the signs and avoid the peril before
it arrives again.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.600
The third film contains many references to
the iconic tragedy that kicked off the series,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.600
Flight 180.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.389
The roller coaster that crashes in the third
movie is called Devil’s Flight, a reference

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:17.720
to Alex seeing a luggage vehicle with the
devil’s number before boarding his flight

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.720
in the original.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.949
Before getting on the ride, Wendy and Kevin
even line up in Row 6.

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:28.520
Ashley and Ashlyn go to Phoenix Tanning Salon,
whose phone number is listed as 570-555-0180.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.920
And when Wendy and Kevin are on the way to
the fast food drive through, there’s a near-accident

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.620
with a truck from Penn State Towing and Recovery,
whose phone number after the area code is

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.430
also 555-0180.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.450
Later on, Ian McKinley operated a forklift,
and in one close up we see that it’s UNIT

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.920
081, the mirror image of 180.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.641
At the end, Wendy boards subway train 081,
and later sees it in the mirror as 180, just

00:00:49.641 --> 00:00:54.570
like how we saw the backside of the sign of
Cafe Miro 81, reading as the number 180 during

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.190
the conclusion of the original.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:01.289
To learn all the hidden secrets of Final Destination
3, including the HUGE CONSPIRACY REGARDING

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:05.607
THE SUBWAY SCENE AT THE END, stick around
to the end of this video.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:10.829
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:13.929
This one has a roller coaster, and that’s
very exciting for me, so I want to hurry up

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:14.929
and get to that.

00:01:14.929 --> 00:01:18.259
But for the third installment, the series
was handed back over to James Wong with a

00:01:18.259 --> 00:01:19.579
G, who directed the first one.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.139
I’d say he immediately got the series back
on track.

00:01:22.139 --> 00:01:23.850
There’s irony in that sentence, I know.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.563
Let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:34.079
The opening credits bring back many of the
themes established, that I’ve discussed

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:35.740
in my episodes on the other movies.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.200
We see a fortune teller, representing the
idea of psychic premonitions, and she has

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.130
tarot cards for Hope, Fate, The Devil and
Death.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.569
We also see a painting of the devil and I
already mentioned the name of the coaster.

00:01:45.569 --> 00:01:49.729
The second movie contained a lot of symbols
of luck, chance and fate all being linked,

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:53.520
and in this one we’re shown a spinning wheel
and a pinball game, both examples of carnival

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.219
games -- games of chance.

00:01:55.219 --> 00:01:58.799
The pinball game has holes labeled as Luck,
Fate and Death respectively.

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:02.590
Another mural depicts “The Electric Sisters”
defying death in twin electric chairs.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:06.259
The last two survivors in this movie end up
being Wendy and her sister, Julie.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.149
There are a lot of pairs in this one in general.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:10.659
We start off with two couples, Ashley and
Ashlyn are a pair.

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:13.790
We’ve got a pair of token goth characters,
MCR and Misery Business.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:17.069
MCR’s real name is Ian McKinley, which pairs
with the name of the town.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:21.069
Devil’s Flight seats in pairs, and there
are a pair of train related accidents: a roller

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:23.129
coaster train and a subway train.

00:02:23.129 --> 00:02:27.099
That roller coaster is Devil’s Flight, which
was filmed on Playland Vancouver’s Corkscrew,

00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:28.730
whose sign makes a cameo right here.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:32.739
I find it hilarious that the coaster they
die on is a Vekoma coaster in North America,

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:36.370
because the manufacturer Vekoma doesn’t
have a great reputation on this continent.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.740
They’re the ones who do all the Boomerang
coasters and have made some infamously rough

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.810
suspended looping coasters… or SLCs.

00:02:43.116 --> 00:02:44.116
“Vekoma SLCs.

00:02:44.116 --> 00:02:46.739
A horror of a word in the coaster community.”

00:02:46.739 --> 00:02:52.159
“And one of the things I learned was how
horrible the Vekoma SLCs apparently are.”

00:02:52.159 --> 00:02:55.269
“This has been a step by step guide to riding
Vekoma SLCs.

00:02:55.269 --> 00:02:59.760
As you can see, we only got to step number
five, because everyone is dead.”

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.590
Devil’s Flight is not an SLC though, it’s
a model called Corkscrew with Bayerncurve.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.269
Not particularly exciting, so for the movie,
more elements were added with CGI.

00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:12.849
“Since we don’t have an actual roller
coaster that has a 360° loop, we’re recreating

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:14.650
it on a stage.”

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:18.359
This made it look less like a Vekoma and more
like an Arrow Dynamics looping coaster.

00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:22.230
In particular, it looks a lot like Viper at
Six Flags Magic Mountain, but the theming

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:26.480
also reminds me of a different looping coaster
by Arrow Dynamics, Demon at Six Flags Great

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.140
America and California’s Great America,
which happens to be my first inverting roller

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.140
coaster.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.750
Final Destination 3 introduced a new concept
where the signs about each character’s death

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.389
could be derived from the last photo that
person appeared in.

00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:40.730
When we first meet the protagonist Wendy,
she’s taking pictures for her school’s

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.780
yearbook as her friends ride the freefall
ride, High Dive, but when she reviews the

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.450
snapshot, the letter V is off, making the
text say “High Die” which is still a better

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.010
title than Hellraiser 7.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:53.340
The next line also foreshadows what’s about
to go down.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.075
KEVIN: “That was intense man.

00:03:55.075 --> 00:03:57.487
To feel how it would be to just crash and
burn like that.”

00:03:57.487 --> 00:04:00.000
WENDY: “Yeah, yeah, maybe for you but our
lives are actually going somewhere.”

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.510
Wendy’s boyfriend also suggests that eating
junk food before going on Devil’s Flight

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.510
“might kill him.”

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:09.189
To this point, the opening disasters both
took place on May 13th.

00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:12.670
We never do see the exact date of the roller
coaster accident, but I do think it makes sense

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:16.180
that it’s also May 13th because they’re
at the amusement park as part of their school’s

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:19.340
grad night, an event that would typically
take place in mid-May.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:23.060
At the midway, Wendy photographs her classmate
Lewis trying a test of strength, but he’s

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.389
a little too strong and knocks the head clean
off.

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:29.020
This is a sign of how Death would get to him
during a different test of strength in his

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.789
football team’s weight room, where his head
ends up being crushed by a pair of weights.

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:35.370
Then, our characters head for Devil’s Flight.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.345
JASON: “What’s wrong?”

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.750
WENDY: I was having that feeling like Déjà vu, you
know.”

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.250
No Wendy, you’ve got the wrong Vekoma coaster.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.780
This is Devil’s Flight.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:49.479
The voice of the titular devil is the voice
of the coroner from the first two movies,

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:50.479
William Bludworth.

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:54.360
I did a whole video explaining why he might
be here, so check that one out if you’re interested.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.590
In line, the school’s super-super senior
Frankie is seen with a mudflap girl necklace,

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:02.789
an icon commonly associated with truckers,
which foreshadows his eventual death by runaway

00:05:02.789 --> 00:05:03.789
truck.

00:05:03.789 --> 00:05:07.010
At the end of the line, Jason and Kevin
both want the front row, so a coin flip ends

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:11.169
up deciding for them, once again tying the
idea of fate to luck and chance.

00:05:11.169 --> 00:05:12.470
So they all get on the ride.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.220
Who comes off a coaster looking like that?

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.360
The harnesses come down, and it’s clear
that Lewis is a coaster enthusiast.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.560
“What’s up man, I’m good.”

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.860
We call that stapling.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.930
“And almost nothing ruins a great ride more
than being stapled into your seat.”

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:31.169
There would be more signs, coincidences too
uncanny to be coincidences, easter eggs and

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:34.509
more after Devil’s Flight departed from
the station.

00:05:34.509 --> 00:05:36.198
“Here we go!”

00:05:36.198 --> 00:05:36.989
“Yeah!

00:05:36.989 --> 00:05:38.280
Let’s do it baby!”

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.000
“We have to get off of here…”

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.289
In Final Destination 2, I pointed out how
the leaked transmission fluid kind of looked

00:05:53.289 --> 00:05:57.770
like blood, and similar image is used when
the hydraulics get ruptured, giving the appearance

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:58.770
of dripping blood.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:00.419
Before the train departs, this happens.

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:06.120
“Dare you to flash me those sweet sweet
titties when we go through the loop.”

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.820
Frankie, not only is that highly inappropriate,
but do you see these over the shoulder restraints?

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:12.110
How would they do that??

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:15.690
As the ride ascends the lift hill, you can
spot a nearby top spin ride called Hell’s

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:19.050
Gate, another one of the many demon references
I’ve pointed out in this franchise.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.870
Jay and Carrie are on the first car that derails.

00:06:28.569 --> 00:06:32.069
Lewis flies out of his harness, and MCR and
Misery Business are dropped from the top of

00:06:32.069 --> 00:06:33.490
the loop where the train is stuck.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.820
I mentioned the comparison to Demon earlier.

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:39.650
This part may be inspired by an incident that
occurred on Demon in 1998, where the train

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:43.030
got stuck on the top of one of the ride’s
two vertical loops and had to be evacuated

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.210
by the fire department.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.740
Nobody died during this incident, but it still
gave birth to an urban legend about a kid

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:52.000
who supposedly didn’t meet the height requirement
and fell to his death when it got stuck; which

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.199
growing up in Chicagoland and going to the
park as a kid, I believed for several years.

00:06:56.199 --> 00:07:00.060
When Wendy comes out of the vision, she freaks
out and causes 7 people including herself

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.330
to get off the ride.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:05.629
Seven and thirteen come up a lot, the lucky
and unlucky numbers, and seven was the same

00:07:05.629 --> 00:07:07.620
number of survivors from Flight 180.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.780
In Wendy’s room there’s a picture of 7
stick figures holding hands.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.610
Looks like it belongs in the movie Us.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.389
Some time after the accident, Wendy clears
out her locker.

00:07:15.389 --> 00:07:19.370
Her locker number is D-073, a sign about the
next pair of deaths that would occur when

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:24.120
Ashley and Ashlyn turn up the thermostat in
the tanning salon to 73°, causing the machines

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:25.610
to overheat and malfunction.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.800
In the last movie I mentioned how Evan Lewis’s
Pontiac Firebird was one of the signals of

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.580
the apartment fire that led to his fate.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:35.680
A phoenix is a mythological bird said to die
in a burst of flames and then it’s successor

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.360
is born from the ashes.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:40.330
Ashley and Ashlyn are both names that be shortened
to Ash.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:44.889
When referred to in plural, they are the Ashes,
and they both die in flames at Phoenix Tanning

00:07:44.889 --> 00:07:45.389
Salon.

00:07:45.389 --> 00:07:49.140
Ashlyn forgets her iPod, so they listen to
one of the CDs available at the salon, so

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:52.789
Ashley picks out Have A Nice Decade, Volume
6 -- there’s the devil’s number again.

00:07:52.789 --> 00:07:54.893
The song they listen to is Love Rollercoaster.

00:07:54.893 --> 00:07:55.550
Get it?

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:56.969
Because they were supposed to die on a roller
coaster?

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.469
So clever.

00:07:58.469 --> 00:08:01.979
But like Demon, this song has its own ominous
urban legend attached to it.

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:05.000
The story goes that the scream heard during
the instrumental 

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:09.177
🎵 Love Rollercoaster - Ohio Players 🎵

00:08:09.177 --> 00:08:11.930
is actually the scream of a woman being murdered.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:15.759
Other versions of the legend say it’s actually
audio of her falling off of a roller coaster.

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:19.500
While Ashley and Ashlyn are getting some color
for their funeral, Wendy misses a few signs

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.180
in her room, like a sticky note with writing
on it that says “Books To Die For.”

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.220
There’s also a monkey doll that’s hanging
onto the dresser in a similar way to how MCR

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.560
and Misery Business held onto the coaster
for dear life in her vision.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:32.940
She notices the photo of Ash and Ash, and
the lens flare makes it look as if they are

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.730
burning in a fire, so she tries to call and
warn them.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:39.453
ASHLEY: “Hello?”
WENDY: “Hey Ashley, it’s Wendy.”

00:08:39.453 --> 00:08:40.414
ASHLEY: .Psyche!

00:08:40.414 --> 00:08:41.368
Leave a message.”

00:08:41.368 --> 00:08:44.430
“HA! GOT EEM! HA!”

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.940
At their funeral, the same exact music from
the Flight 180 memorial plays; it’s called

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.530
Hundered Grand by Pete Atherton.

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.500
I believe it was made specifically for the
movie.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.860
After the ceremony, Wendy pulls out a photo
of regular Abraham Lincoln.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:58.200
But basically Wendy says she believes her
photos from the night of the accident will

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.330
contain signs, just as these photos taken
before historical disasters seem to.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.290
I know the whole images that precede unfortunate
events has become a meme at this point, but

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:09.070
I can assure you she did not print out these
photos for meme purposes.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:13.660
They go to a fast food joint called Andy’s
to talk about it some more, and try to decipher

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.722
Frankie’s picture.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:18.190
“Spongebob lives underwater.”

00:09:19.775 --> 00:09:21.184
“It’s so sad that you know that.”

00:09:21.184 --> 00:09:21.940
What?

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:22.940
Everyone knows that.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.430
It’s right in the theme song.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.635
“Who lives in a pineapple under the sea?

00:09:28.635 --> 00:09:33.728
"Thank you so much Mr. Krabs. You're a life-saver. Go see Patrick."

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.620
While they’re analysing the picture, a Hice
Pale Ale truck passes behind them.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.980
Those of you who saw my FD2 episode will remember
the drinking Hice Pale Ale truck driver during

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:45.470
Kimberly’s premonition of the accident,
a brand named after stunt coordinator Freddie

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:46.470
Hice.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:49.170
We don’t know if this driver survived the
real version of the pile up, but I like to

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.390
think it’s the same guy.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.510
This truck nearly gets Wendy and Kevin killed
when it blocks them in before the next accident.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:57.890
Wendy first suspects something is wrong when
the order screen glitches out and the word

00:09:57.890 --> 00:09:58.890
“control” disappears.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:02.530
It’s essentially telling Wendy she’s losing
control of the situation.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:03.416
Because as we know…

00:10:03.417 --> 00:10:05.358
"I mean, you know I'm such a control freak."

00:10:05.358 --> 00:10:09.274
"The real fear with these rides comes from the feeling of having no control."

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:10.780
"I'm usually such a control freak."

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:12.048
"...sense of having no control."

00:10:12.048 --> 00:10:14.580
"Well it's nice to see that things haven't made you any less of a control freak."

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:18.790
Then the car radio starts playing Turn Around
Look At Me, originally by Glen Campbell.

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:23.454
🎵 There is someone walking behind you… 🎵

00:10:23.454 --> 00:10:26.620
A clue that the danger is going to come from
behind them.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:29.930
The first pair of deaths came during the song
“Love Rollercoaster” and this one would

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:31.490
have a coaster reference as well.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:34.940
The runaway truck that would eventually take
out Frankie is from Rolling Thunder Moving

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:35.940
and Storage.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.140
Rolling Thunder is fairly common roller coaster
name, but the biggest Rolling Thunder was

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:41.250
the one at Six Flags Great Adventure.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:44.870
In 1981, a park employee who failed to secure
the safety bar fell to his death during a

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:45.870
test run.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.310
The truck barrels towards the Andy’s drive
through after it’s left unattended and rolls

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:53.522
down a big hill, converting potential energy
into kinetic energy, like a roller coaster.

00:10:53.522 --> 00:10:56.750
“ A roller coaster is just elemental physics.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:59.510
A conversion of potential energy to kinetic
energy.”

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:03.350
The truck also features blue white and red
stripes, the colors of the French flag that

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.610
are seen in stripes on the Volée Flight 180
aircraft, the bus that struck Terry Chaney,

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.730
and the train that ended Billy Hitchcock.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:13.310
With just over half of the Devil’s Flight
survivors remaining, Wendy and Kevin would

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:18.293
try to decipher the rest of the photos, and
in them, we can find even more Things You Missed.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.880
As they review the remaining photos from the
night of the accident, Wendy and Kevin look

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.180
for any potential clues about the next death.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:36.060
Wendy had already seen Jason’s photo, where
it looks like his head is about to be struck

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:37.060
by a roller coaster.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:40.870
I’ve got a similar photo from 2017, so if
anyone knows how I’m gonna die, please get

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:41.870
in contact.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:44.990
She also found Frankie’s picture where his
head looks like it could be hit by a spinning

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.370
fan-blade that looks similar to the motor
that took him out not long ago.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.496
They figure that the next victim will be Lewis,
but they struggle to determine the cause of

00:11:51.496 --> 00:11:52.095
death.

00:11:52.095 --> 00:11:55.130
They eventually decide that this Swirling
Dervish guy could represent Lewis’s football

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:58.460
team and the guy flexing his muscles might
be a sign that the accident occurs in the

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.460
weight room.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.040
They fail to consider how the Sultan’s scimitars
play into the equation.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.040
However, when they get there they do discover
a pair of swords, along with the motivational

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.881
text: “what doesn’t kill you makes you
stronger,” a callback to Kevin’s line

00:12:08.881 --> 00:12:11.710
before going on Devil’s Flight.

00:12:11.711 --> 00:12:13.295
JASON: "Before riding Devil's Flight? Yeah, that might kill me."

00:12:13.295 --> 00:12:14.295
KEVIN: “No!

00:12:14.295 --> 00:12:18.740
What doesn't kill you makes you stronger,
man.”

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.390
There’s also a callback to the first movie.

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:24.450
You may remember during Tod’s accident there
was nearly a moment where he could have been

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:28.390
electrocuted when he plugs in the radio just
before the leaked water reached his feet.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.250
This time, the leak comes from the water fountain,
and the radio is a boombox.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:35.210
Instead of playing Rocky Mountain High, the
song of choice is appropriately titled “Killing

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.360
Time” by Hed Planet Earth.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.760
If Final Destination 3 was made today, maybe
they would have just done a cover of Rocky

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:41.890
Mountain High called Rocky Mountain Construction.

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:45.820
This seems like as good a time as any to bring
up constant use of water as part of Death’s

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:46.820
designs.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.020
Almost all the deaths in the last two movies
had water or liquid involved in some way and

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:53.470
we see it again here: the leaked hydraulic
fluid on the ride, the dripping beverage at

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:56.950
the tanning salon, this water fountain at
the gym and the spilled All Purpose Glass

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.580
Cleaner that the forklift slipped on at the
hardware store.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:02.700
After being unable to save Lewis, they go
back to the car and they’re now just wearing

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:03.700
Sultan’s merch?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:06.700
Sure, they just saw a guy’s head explode
but who could resist hitting the gift shop

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:07.730
on the way out?

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:11.880
I guess there is a valid reason, since their
clothes got spattered in Lewis’s guts, but

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.110
still seems kind of funny.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:16.490
Then they have this moment together, please
do not smash your best friend’s girl a week

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:17.830
after his death my dude.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.830
OK good.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:19.830
They leave.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.570
Another running gag that I brought up when
covering the first two Final Destinations

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:26.110
was that many of the characters were named
after classic horror movie icons.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.640
This time we had many more.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:31.070
Wendy and Julie Christensen were named after
Benjamin Christensen; Kevin Fischer after

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:35.270
Terrence Fischer, Jason Wise perhaps named
after Robert Wise who made the original The

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:39.700
Haunting, Carrie Dreyer after Carl Theodore
Dreyer (she may also be related to Blake Dreyer

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:45.070
from Flight 180, Lewis Romero after George
A Romero, Ashley Freund after Karl Freund,

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:49.330
Ashlyn Halperin after Victor Halperin and
the two cops Clark and Polanski, who are named

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.030
after Bob Clark and Roman Polanski.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:54.550
There’s also a security guy named Bludworth,
a reference to the coroner from the previous

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:55.981
movies, William Bludworth.

00:13:55.981 --> 00:13:58.718
Ian and Erin also have nicknames for each
other, Zip and Pip...

00:13:58.751 --> 00:14:01.848
ERIN: "Zip? It's Pip. Have you cut those plywood orders yet?"

00:14:01.848 --> 00:14:06.880
...which are the names of these two in the 1932 horror classic: Freaks,
kind of a self-aware joke about them being

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:07.890
the gothic pair.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:11.160
There’s also a new theme introduced in this
one, where there’s a common nomenclature

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.440
for all the exits on the subway, but I’ll
get to that a little bit later on in the video.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:19.170
Next up on Death’s hitlist is our good friends
Misery Business and MCR, who never told us

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.180
what he does for a living.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:23.200
Despite the nickname I’ve given him, he
doesn’t work in a cubicle, but rather, at

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:27.450
a hardware store, which happens to be filled
with a lot of… not so conventional weapons.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.760
If we take a look at the photo for these two, there
are a couple of things to note.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.110
The picture is taken at the midway, and the
lettering overhead says “Test Your Skill”,

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:37.680
but you’ll notice that the letter S is kind
of receded into the dark, and the result is

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.940
just the word KILL.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:42.110
These things that are pointed down at him
are the same shape as the giant Tricentennial

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.181
sign that crushes him at the end of the movie.

00:14:44.181 --> 00:14:46.700
The photo also shows him holding a gun up
to his girlfriend’s face.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:50.190
He doesn’t end up being the one to pull
the trigger on her, but it is his nail gun

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.740
that fires off and ultimately does her in,
and she passes on while holding her hand

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.970
up in the same pose that she does in the image.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:59.550
In the first movie, there were constant allusions
to France, and more specifically, people who

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:03.490
passed away in France, and Ian’s mockery
of the supposed death signals makes reference

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:04.490
to that.

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:10.000
“How come when a guy dies of a plain heart
attack, no one goes like, ‘Oh wow, he was

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:14.895
eating french toast, when Princess Diana died
in Paris, and then he saw the funeral on TV

00:15:14.895 --> 00:15:15.912
and now he’s dead.”

00:15:15.912 --> 00:15:19.440
Before I get on to the last two disaster scenes
of the movie, I want to circle back to something

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.720
I touched on earlier: luck, chance and fate.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:25.690
I’ve already gone over several examples
of references to luck and characters having

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.920
lucky charms, but there are actually even
more that are associated with these three

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.480
characters that make it to the end.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:33.920
Wendy’s sister Julie has a bracelet given
to her by her grandmother, and in one line

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:36.670
we learn that she actually considers it to be a
good luck charm.

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:42.380
“Wen, so I’m meeting some guys at that
Centennial things and I could really use my

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:45.430
good luck… bracelet...”

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:49.380
When she wakes up, she realizes that her sister
is in danger, so she rushes to the tri-centennial

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.380
to try to save her.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:52.080
On the way, she crosses paths with…

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.550
Bloody hell it’s Sirius Black!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.540
No wait, it’s just a wolf.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:58.980
But wolves are considered to be a symbol of
good luck in Mongolian folklore.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:02.730
Then at the festival, we see a blacksmith
smelting an iron horseshoe, which, as I mentioned

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.240
when I talked about FD2, is another good luck
charm.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.620
Then, briefly skipping ahead to the final
scene on the train, there's a poster for Discovery

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:13.110
State Lottery, advertising a potential lucky
payday, a scratch card lotto with the text:

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:16.920
this could be your lucky day, and in Wendy’s
final vision, she breaks her leg -- the phrase

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:19.230
‘break a leg’ is another way of saying
good luck.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:22.670
At the beginning of the tri-centennial celebration
scene, we’re given a sort of quick recap

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.150
of all the disasters so far.

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:27.640
We’re shown a horseback rider to represent
the riders of the roller coaster; a fiery

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:31.050
grill to represent the burning girls in the
tanning salon; we cut to Wendy hearing the

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.790
song that played before Frankie’s demise,
we see some colonial men marching with swords

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:38.680
to represent the swords that destroyed the
weight machine that offed Lewis, and MCR shows

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.570
up, it was his nail gun that took out Erin.

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:42.730
For some reason he’s acting like iDubbbz.

00:16:43.514 --> 00:16:47.370
“Hey, I’m just celebrating our town’s
tri-centennial.”

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.872
“What a day!

00:16:48.872 --> 00:16:50.702
What a lovely day!”

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:55.260
Kevin chases about a couple of kids with sparklers
in a scene very reminiscent of Clear at the

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:59.610
gas station in Final Destination 2, and MCR suffers a fate that looked almost exactly

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.920
like that of Tim Carpenter in that same movie.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:04.080
I just don’t get why neither of them don't try
to move.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.459
I guess he really just wanted to go headfirst
for Halos.

00:17:06.459 --> 00:17:09.893
You know he may have had a bulletproof heart,
but he most certainly didn’t have signproof

00:17:09.893 --> 00:17:10.440
head.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:15.329
Like the FD1 finale in Paris, the subway scene
would be the grand finale of Final Destination

00:17:15.329 --> 00:17:19.812
3, and it holds more secrets than any other
scene so far in the franchise.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:33.270
Five months after the main events of the movie,
Wendy is in college, thinking that her, her

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:36.360
sister and Kevin are now safe from Death’s
onslaught.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:39.630
Just as the opening took place on a roller
coaster train, the finale would go down on

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:40.639
a subway train.

00:17:40.639 --> 00:17:44.240
The advertisements plastered upon the walls
and ceiling are looming reminders of the tragedies

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:46.690
that befell Wendy’s classmates just that
summer.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:50.169
We see the Slushee ad, the same forbidden
drink that Ashley snuck into the tanning room,

00:17:50.169 --> 00:17:52.870
which ultimately dripped into the machinery
and caused their disaster.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.720
Of course, I already mentioned the inclusion
of the Phoenix Tanning Company.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.320
There’s a promo for Build It.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:01.570
This is the hardware store where Misery Business
wasn’t careful enough and uh… became a

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:02.679
misguided ghost.

00:18:02.679 --> 00:18:06.470
Then there’s one for Andy’s, the fast
food drive through where Frankie drove in,

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:07.470
but not out.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.309
Then there’s Montgomery and Glick.

00:18:09.309 --> 00:18:12.220
This one’s actually a real company, and
I wouldn’t be surprised if this is the tax

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.850
firm of choice for some of the crew.

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:16.049
But the important part to note here, is the
slogan.

00:18:16.049 --> 00:18:17.950
“There’s no escaping death and taxes.”

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:20.830
The saying usually goes “there are only
two certainties in life, death and taxes,”

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:24.879
so the “no escape” thing is a nice Final
Destination twist on the old phrase.

00:18:24.879 --> 00:18:28.380
Another poster advertises a product called
Cheez-y-Chums, which is made by Wohlgemuth

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:29.380
Fine Foods.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:32.370
That’s a reference to Final Destination
3’s art director, Tony Wohlgemuth.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:37.000
There’s also a new product called Blaze
Unsweetened something, perhaps another clue

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.260
of the fiery crash that would soon occur.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.330
The one I find to be the most interesting
though, is the rail map.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:44.693
I noticed something was up when I heard this.

00:18:44.693 --> 00:18:45.693
Roll it.

00:18:46.297 --> 00:18:50.211
“This is Booth Street.

00:18:50.211 --> 00:18:52.680
Next stop is Oswald.

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:53.959
End of the line.

00:18:53.959 --> 00:18:57.500
Next stop is the end of the line.”

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:00.299
Booth and Oswald are both assassins of American
presidents.

00:19:00.299 --> 00:19:03.750
John Wilkes Booth is the guy who shot Regular
Abraham Lincoln, as Wendy explained earlier

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:07.360
in the movie, and Lee Harvey Oswald is the
man believed to have sniped John F Keneddy.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:09.799
That got me thinking about the rail map here.

00:19:09.799 --> 00:19:11.490
We see a stop at Ruby Drive.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:15.419
Jack Ruby is the guy that killed Lee Harvey
Oswald 2 days later in retaliation.

00:19:15.419 --> 00:19:16.980
The next stop is McVeigh.

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:20.379
Timothy McVeigh was responsible for the Oklahoma
City bombings in 1995.

00:19:20.379 --> 00:19:24.379
When he was arrested, he was wearing a t-shirt
with a picture of Abraham Lincoln on it and the

00:19:24.379 --> 00:19:28.309
words sic semper tyrannis -- allegedly the
same words that John Wilkes Booth shouted

00:19:28.309 --> 00:19:30.799
in the Ford Theater before executing Lincoln.

00:19:30.799 --> 00:19:32.059
Then there’s 63rd Street.

00:19:32.059 --> 00:19:34.879
John F Kennedy was assassinated in 1963.

00:19:34.879 --> 00:19:35.940
After that, there’s Hidell.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:39.799
Hidell was the alias used by Lee Harvey Oswald
when he bought the rifle used to fire upon

00:19:39.799 --> 00:19:40.799
John F Kennedy.

00:19:40.799 --> 00:19:44.179
On the other side of the map, starting with
the orange line, is another stop is called

00:19:44.179 --> 00:19:45.179
Jim Jones.

00:19:45.179 --> 00:19:48.620
This was a cult leader who organized a major
deadly crime in Jonestown, Guyana.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.840
One of the other stops is called Jonestown
Transfer.

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:53.470
The next stop on orange looks like is says
Hinkey.

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:57.360
This could be a misspelling of the surname
of George Warren Hickey Jr., the secret service

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:00.750
agent who was in the car behind John F Kennedy
the day he was shot.

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:04.679
Some conspiracy theorists believe Hickey Jr.
is actually the one who took out Kennedy.

00:20:04.679 --> 00:20:06.170
The orange line ends at Hubbard.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:08.210
James Hubbard was a murderer from Alabama
in the 70s.

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:11.440
There are a couple other stops on the other
side of the orange line that are a little

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:12.440
harder to make out.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:15.899
It looks like this one says Manchester, a
reference to Trevor Hardy, and English killer

00:20:15.899 --> 00:20:19.499
who was nicknamed The Beast of Manchester;
and this one says Berkowitz.

00:20:19.499 --> 00:20:23.850
That would be David Berkowitz, the man responsible
for several shooting in 1976 New York.

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:26.200
Moving over to the green line, there’s Bundy.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.840
That’s named after Ted Bundy, one of the
biggest serial criminals in American history.

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:32.549
I already mentioned Jonestown Transfer, so
next up is Czolgosz.

00:20:32.549 --> 00:20:36.050
Now I have to admit, at first I thought this
guy was pretty cool for having the letters

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:40.330
CZ at the beginning of his name, but then I found out that
he’s not as cool as me, because Leon Czolgosz

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:42.880
was the assassin of American president William
McKinley.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:46.820
That’s when it all clicked for me, cause
when you watch Final Destination 3, one name

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:48.980
you’ll hear over and over is McKinley.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:52.321
Their town is named McKinley, there’s also
a McKinley street on the subway map, the theme

00:20:52.321 --> 00:20:56.970
park was McKinley park, the school was McKinley
high and MCR’s real name was Ian McKinley.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:21:00.529
With this in mind, I thought back to the first
movie and started making even more connections.

00:21:00.529 --> 00:21:05.010
Mt. Abraham, New York and Mt. Abraham High
School -- both were probably named for Abraham

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:05.510
Lincoln.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:08.080
Flight 180 also took off out of JFK airport.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.890
The license plate of Carter’s car had the
letters RFK.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:14.610
That stands for Robert F Kennedy, JFK’s
brother who was also assassinated.

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:19.190
The next green line stop is Carcano, a reference
to the type of rifle Lee Harvey Oswald used.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.190
After that is Gein.

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:21.190
Ed Gein.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.389
The butcher of Plainfield, Wisconsin.

00:21:22.389 --> 00:21:23.389
Applewhite.

00:21:23.389 --> 00:21:26.299
That’s Marshall Applewhite, another cult
leader who did horrible stuff and claimed

00:21:26.299 --> 00:21:27.429
39 lives.

00:21:27.429 --> 00:21:28.679
Finally we have the Red line.

00:21:28.679 --> 00:21:32.200
And that starts with Earl Way, a reference
to James Earl Ray, the man who took out Martin

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.539
Luther King Jr.

00:21:33.539 --> 00:21:34.039
Next stop.

00:21:34.039 --> 00:21:34.564
Koresh.

00:21:34.564 --> 00:21:35.738
Another cult leader.

00:21:35.738 --> 00:21:36.668
This one’s from Texas.

00:21:36.668 --> 00:21:37.581
Really bad stuff.

00:21:37.581 --> 00:21:38.459
At least 20 victims.

00:21:38.459 --> 00:21:39.598
Next stop.

00:21:39.598 --> 00:21:40.285
Mambro.

00:21:40.285 --> 00:21:45.019
Franchesca Mambro was Italian bomber who took
96 victims in Rome in 1980.

00:21:45.019 --> 00:21:46.240
Next stop: Chapman.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:49.559
Mark David Chapman isn’t just a banger of
a Mindless Self Indulgence song, he was another

00:21:49.559 --> 00:21:53.259
assassin from Texas whose jealousy of the
Beatles went too far and he unfortunately

00:21:53.259 --> 00:21:54.899
ended the life of John Lennon.

00:21:54.899 --> 00:21:58.340
There are a lot of crazy theories about secret
messages hidden in Beatles songs during the

00:21:58.340 --> 00:21:59.340
aftermath of this.

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:02.330
I’m not gonna get into it in this video,
but I will just point out that Love Rollercoaster

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:05.590
isn’t the only song referenced by this movie
with an urban legend behind it.

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:08.549
As long as I’m on the topic of dead rock
stars here, I’m just gonna point out that

00:22:08.549 --> 00:22:12.370
Wendy has a bobblehead of Joey Ramone in her
room, so maybe that ties into this somehow

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:13.370
as well.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:16.029
And my final thing that I’d like to point
out is the end credits music.

00:22:16.029 --> 00:22:19.159
After the roller coaster crash, we heard the
song Love Rollercoaster.

00:22:19.159 --> 00:22:22.299
And after the train crash to end the movie,
the credits rolled accompanied by a cover

00:22:22.299 --> 00:22:23.990
of the song “Love Train”.

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:27.669
If you’re familiar with this song, you may
know the original artist is The O’Jays,

00:22:27.669 --> 00:22:32.070
which gives us one more alleged killer reference,
as OJ Simpson was suspected of taking out

00:22:32.070 --> 00:22:33.990
his wife in 1994.

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:37.549
Click the video on the left for more even
more Things You Missed in the Final Destination

00:22:37.549 --> 00:22:38.549
franchise.

00:22:38.549 --> 00:22:40.929
Coming up next, I’ll be covering movies
4 and 5, so make sure you don’t miss it

00:22:40.929 --> 00:22:45.450
by subscribing to CZsWorld for new horrors
every week, RING the deathbell to select all

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:47.789
notifications, and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:22:47.789 --> 00:22:50.020
Assuming we both survive.

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:53.120
If you want to beat death, use a facemask
and social distancing.

00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:53.990
PLEASE.

